name: Review stays coherent and interactive while a finite writer updates another finding
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: NODE_OPTIONS KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/review_snapshot.py @TMP_TARGET @ART prepare
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: findings
require-live-snap: 25 rows 1-500 of 800 | first-page
nav-mode:
keys: C-n
require-live-snap: 25 501-800/800 | later-page
paste-file: @ART/open.txt
require-live-snap: 15 open F- | open-draft
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 SELECTED FINDING | selected-owned-row
expect-echo-within: 300 retained-concurrent-review-draft
live-snap: retained-draft
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/review_snapshot.py @TMP_TARGET @ART start
wait: 2
live-snap: writing-review
expect: retained-concurrent-review-draft
expect-not: Ledger refresh failed
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/review_snapshot.py @TMP_TARGET @ART active
ask: Does Review keep the later page, selected finding and composer draft while genuine external ledger writes continue, with no refresh failure or implicit decision?
keys: C-u
submit: decision deferred J155 owned unchanged finding deferred during updates
nav-mode:
keys: g
require-live-snap: 25 J155 owned unchanged finding deferred during updates | decision-during-writes
expect: 501-800/800
expect-not: Ledger refresh failed
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/review_snapshot.py @TMP_TARGET @ART decided
ask: Does the explicit decision remain bound to the unchanged selected observation while another finding changes, with no verdict borrowed from a new generation?
resize: 160x48
live-snap: review-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: review-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: review-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: review-60x20
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 SELECTED FINDING | narrow-detail
resize: 40x12
live-snap: review-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: detail-page-1
keys: NPage
live-snap: detail-page-2
expect: recorded: deferred
keys: NPage
live-snap: detail-page-3
expect-not: Ledger refresh failed
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/review_snapshot.py @TMP_TARGET @ART decided
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/review_snapshot.py @TMP_TARGET @ART stop
keys: q
require-live-snap: 20 501-800/800 | later-page-restored
ask: Do narrow and wide layouts retain the same evidence and allow detail/list navigation while the owned writer remains bounded and stops explicitly?
resize: 120x36
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: findings
require-live-snap: 25 rows 1-500 of 800 | recovered-first
nav-mode:
keys: C-n
require-live-snap: 25 501-800/800 | recovered-later
paste-file: @ART/open.txt
require-live-snap: 15 open F- | recovered-open
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 J155 owned unchanged finding deferred during updates | recovered-decision
expect-not: Ledger refresh failed
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/review_snapshot.py @TMP_TARGET @ART recovered
ask: Does no-color restart preserve the exact human decision and all synthetic observation history without source changes, model requests or scanner work?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
